# Trivy vulnerability suppression file for CppCheckDocker.
# Format: one CVE ID per line, followed by an inline comment justifying the
# suppression (rationale, expiry date, upstream fix reference).
#
# Suppressions must be reviewed at each release (see CCD-SPL2-001 §4).
# Empty entries are not permitted.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-99999   # False positive: cppcheck build does not use the affected
#                    # code path; upstream fix expected in cppcheck 2.22.
